The Android API artifact supplies symbols and throwing SDK stubs. It is not an
Android operating system or an ART runtime. No subscribed JAR, decrypted code,
remote scripts, credentials or runtime databases are included in source control.

Additional JVM host WebDAV libraries (not dependencies found in the audited
official TVBox APK): sardine-android 0.4 and Simple XML 2.7.1, Apache-2.0.
Sardine's v0.4 Gradle declaration uses OkHttp 3.11.0; this host reuses its already
pinned OkHttp 3.12.11 and Okio 2.8.0 instead of adding a second HTTP stack. The
provider helper signatures match the real library. This binding supplies actual
WebDAV operations for JVM class resolution; it is not a claim that the APK
contains this version, or that Android and host WebDAV behavior is identical.
Sardine's JitPack AAR is verified before its exact classes.jar is extracted;
the archive, extracted JAR, POM and source/license provenance are independently
pinned in runtime.json and licenses/sardine-android-0.4/provenance.json. The
JitPack SHA-1 comes from the same repository and is not a separate authenticity
signature. Simple XML's Maven Central SHA-1 and local SHA-256 are retained.
The JDK supplies StAX; obsolete optional StAX/XPP3 binaries are not installed.

ZXing core 3.3.0: Apache-2.0. The immutable TVBoxOS reference app/build.gradle
declares this exact version. It supplies genuine barcode encoding/decoding,
Reed-Solomon error correction and ReaderException/ChecksumException ABI after an
observed Wogg initialization reached the missing ChecksumException on NAS.
The complete Maven Central JAR, published SHA-1, local SHA-256 and byte size are
pinned in runtime.json. The versioned module/parent POMs, upstream tag LICENSE
and provenance are retained under licenses. No QR stub or success shortcut is
introduced; provider execution and final NAS validation are reported separately.
